Here is a concise summary for your notes.

Docker Setup Summary – Ecommerce Platform
Goal

Run infrastructure/supporting services on Docker and business services locally.

Architecture:

Docker:
Postgres
Config Server
Eureka Server
API Gateway

Local (IntelliJ):
Product Service
User Service
Order Service

Benefits:

Less IntelliJ load
Better laptop performance
Automatic startup order
One-command infra startup
Easier logs and management

----------------------------------------
Overall Flow

Startup dependency flow:

Postgres
    ↓
Config Server
    ↓
Eureka Server
    ↓
API Gateway
    ↓
Local Services (Product/User/Order)

Compose health checks ensure proper ordering.
-----------------------------------------------
Dockerfile Setup

Each dockerized service contains:

Location:

same level as pom.xml

Example:

config-server/
├── Dockerfile
├── .dockerignore
├── pom.xml
└── src/

Dockerfile pattern:

FROM eclipse-temurin:21-jdk

WORKDIR /app

COPY target/<jar-name>.jar app.jar

ENTRYPOINT ["java","-jar","app.jar"]

Examples:

Config:

COPY target/ConfigServer-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar config-server.jar

Eureka:

COPY target/EurekaServer-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar eureka-server.jar

Gateway:

COPY target/ApiGateway-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar gateway.jar

Important:

Use:.jar

NOT:.jar.original

--------------------------------------------
.dockerignore

Location:

same folder as Dockerfile

Content:

.git/
.idea/
*.iml
*.log
logs/
README.md

Do NOT ignore:

target/

because Docker needs jar.
---------------------------
Build Images

Inside each service:

Build jar:
mvn clean package
Build image:

Config:

docker build -t config-server .

Eureka:

docker build -t eureka-server .

Gateway:

docker build -t api-gateway .

-t = image tag/name.

. = current folder build context.

Check images:

docker images
--------------------------------

Docker Compose Setup

Folder:

microservices-infra/
└── docker-compose.yml

Purpose:

auto-create network
auto-start services
startup sequencing
one-command infra management

Compose handles:

network creation
container startup
health checks
dependency ordering

No manual:

docker network create
docker run

needed.

---------------------------
Docker Networking Rule
Container → Container

Use:

service/container name

Example:

Gateway:

eureka:
  client:
    service-url:
      defaultZone: http://eureka-server:8761/eureka

Eureka:

spring:
  config:
    import: configserver:http://config-server:8888

Reason:localhost inside container = same container
not another service.
--------------------
Local → Docker

Use:

localhost

Product/User/Order:

Config:

spring:
  config:
    import: configserver:http://localhost:8888

Eureka:

eureka:
  client:
    service-url:
      defaultZone: http://localhost:8761/eureka

Reason:

local machine → exposed Docker ports
------------------------------
Docker → Local

Needed for:

Gateway container → Product/User/Order local

Local services:

eureka:
  instance:
    hostname: host.docker.internal

Otherwise Gateway cannot reach:

localhost

of laptop.
----------------------------

Health Checks / Startup Order

Actuator required.

Dependency:

spring-boot-starter-actuator

Expose:

management:
  endpoints:
    web:
      exposure:
        include: health

Health endpoint:

/actuator/health

Compose waits for:

service_healthy

before starting dependent services.
------------------
Important Commands
Start Infra

From:

microservices-infra

Run:

docker compose up -d

This:

creates network
starts Postgres
waits
starts Config
waits
starts Eureka
starts Gateway
--------------------
Stop Infra
docker compose down

Removes:

containers
network
----------------

Rebuild After Changes

If Dockerfile/config changed:

docker compose down
docker compose build --no-cache
docker compose up -d

--------------
Check Running Containers
docker ps
-----------------
View Logs

Config:

docker logs -f config-server

Eureka:

docker logs -f eureka-server

Gateway:

docker logs -f api-gateway

Postgres:

docker logs -f postgres
-------------------
Git

Commit:

✅ Dockerfile
✅ .dockerignore
✅ docker-compose.yml

Do NOT commit:

❌ target/
❌ jars

Recommended structure:

parent-project/
│
├── config-server/
├── eureka-server/
├── api-gateway/
├── product-service/
├── user-service/
├── order-service/
└── microservices-infra/
    └── docker-compose.yml